From e617fb451b3e0f596ba686331da83188c8e2c2e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:56:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/dma: the PIC32CM JH01/MC00 DMA controller (DMAC U2223)

mchp-dmac-u2223 models the twelve-channel DMAC of the PIC32CM JH01 and
MC00 behind its CHID window, from two probe rounds on MC00 rev A1
silicon (firmware/hello APP=dmacprobe, dmacprobe2): the first descriptor
fetched at enable, one pending request per channel, BEAT/BLOCK/
TRANSACTION actions, beat-level arbitration by level with static or
round-robin priority, the write-back BTCNT updated only when a channel
loses the arbiter, suspends, is disabled or errs, TCMPL at the end of
every transaction, BLOCKACT SUSPEND on any block, RESUME and the skip,
invalid descriptors (TERR + SUSP + FERR, channel left enabled), bus
errors, the software trigger queue, BTCNT 0 as 65536 beats, the CRC-16
and CRC-32 engine in I/O and channel modes with silicon's raw and final
checksum forms, event inputs and outputs, INTPEND, ACTIVE, CHID 12-15
reading channels 8-11, the enable protections and a SWRST that keeps
DBGCTRL. mchp_dmac_set_trigger() serves both DMAC types, so the SoC
wires SERCOM and TC triggers to either. qtest pic32cm-dmac-test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
